message.content:
{
  "summary": "You produced a strong, clearly structured report that balances commercial pressures with professional and public duties. Your stakeholder-specific recommendations and use of external cases are effective. To strengthen the analysis further, clarify what is known about the defect rate and ensure that customer acceptance never substitutes for an adequate safety threshold, particularly where patients may be affected.",
  "next_steps": [
    "Revise Image 1 so customer acceptance cannot by itself justify risks to patients. Specify the professional risk threshold and safeguards required before shipment.",
    "In “The Most Ethical Path,” distinguish the known increase in failure likelihood from the unquantified absolute rate. Identify what testing or evidence Rachel needs to assess the scenario-specific risk.",
    "To strengthen the argument and evidence, give fuller attention to supplier and employee perspectives, and connect any available quantitative defect evidence to your decision rule."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "You meet the Excellent level: the introduction links release pressure to engineering ethics and identifies stakeholder interests and decision authority. To sustain this, continue making clear who is affected and who has authority over each decision.",
    "C2": "You meet the Excellent level with balanced arguments and practical recommendations for several stakeholders. Preserve this balance while making clear that customer acceptance cannot replace a suitable professional safety threshold.",
    "C3": "Your structure and decision rule support a persuasive conclusion. For the Excellent level, develop the comparatively brief supplier and employee perspectives and show systematically how each stakeholder’s interests inform your conclusion.",
    "C4": "Your standards, professional guidance, external cases and evidence support a Very good level. For Excellent, add qualitative and quantitative evidence tied to this server defect, including a clearer account of its likelihood and scenario-specific risks.",
    "C5": "You meet the Excellent level through fluent writing, appropriate sections, effective tables and a decision flowchart, and relevant references. Continue using visual elements and references to support specific points in your argument."
  }
}
